    {
      "argv": ["--help"],
      "exit": 0,
      "verdict": "accepted",
      "stream": "stdout",
      "text": [
        "magpie — a standing review surface for extracting assets from a composite image.",
        "",
        "  open [--title ..] [--intent ..] [--timeout ..] [--restore ..] [--no-open]",
        "                                                spawn a session (opens the browser; --restore <id|path> resumes one, --timeout S); prints {port, session_id, files_dir}",
        "  sessions                                      list saved (resumable) sessions",
        "  tail [--since ..] [--once]                    SSE user events → JSONL (wrap with Monitor); ends itself before Monitor's 30-minute cap with a line naming the next act; a human watching a terminal keeps it open with SPELLBOOK_TAIL_WINDOW_MS=0",
        "  state [--full]                                lean state snapshot (--full for raw)",
        "  say [text...] [--stdin]                       post agent dialogue (text args OR piped stdin with --stdin)",
        "  ask <text...> [--options ..]                  ask the user a question in-thread (--options \"a|b|c\")",
        "  status [on|off] [text...]                     show/hide the \"magpie working\" spinner: status on [text...] | status off",
        "  source <imagePath>                            register the composite under review (computes sha + size)",
        "  discover                                      run discover on the current source → post the breakdown (needs OPENROUTER_API_KEY)",
        "  extract [--ids ..] [--remove] [--alpha ..] [--pad ..] [--model ..] [--label ..]",
        "                                                cut slices (crop-only; --remove adds rembg; --alpha auto|all|none; --pad N)",
        "  export [--ids ..]                             build magpie-bundle.zip (assets/, crops/, manifest.json, gallery.html)",
        "  element-add [--bbox ..] [--name ..] [--type ..]",
        "                                                box a region in source px: --bbox \"x1,y1,x2,y2\"",
        "  element-remove <id>                           retract a boxed region",
        "  cmd [json...] [--stdin]                       POST a raw AgentCommand JSON body (pipe it with --stdin)",
        "  close                                         shut the session (writes its snapshot)",
        "  info                                          the session pointer as JSON",
        "  version                                       this CLI's {name, version} as JSON (alias: --version, -V)",
        "  schema                                        this CLI's machine-readable interface (acc declaration v0)",
        "  help                                          show this message (alias: --help, -h)",
        "  --help | -h | --version | -V  root tokens: help, or {name, version} as JSON",
        "",
        "  extract --model = a rembg model name (isnet-general-use, birefnet-general, …)",
        "  OR a media-forge bg-remove model id (a provider path like",
        "  fal-ai/bria/background/remove — DISCOVER via `media-forge models list`, never",
        "  hardcode); --label sets the version's friendly strip label.",
        "",
        "  Add --session <id> after the verb to target a specific session (default: most",
        "  recent). It is accepted by every verb that acts on a session — not by open,",
        "  sessions, help, version or schema, which do not have one to target.",
        "",
        "  Flags are scoped to their verb: extract's --pad is not accepted by say. A",
        "  rejection lists what the verb it names does accept.",
        "",
        "  Output: magpie prints JSON by default on stdout. Every verb writes ONE JSON",
        "  document there — except `tail`, which is a stream and writes one per line",
        "  (JSONL), and help, which is prose. Liveness and diagnostics go to stderr.",
        "  Failures are one JSON envelope on stderr and exit non-zero (2 = usage,",
        "  1 = internal, 5 = not found, 6 = conflict). `--full` widens the state",
        "  payload; it does not switch formats."
      ]
    },
